2. Mesh & Elevation Catalog (ODbL 1.0)
--------------------------------------
The pre-built X-Plane 12 terrain mesh catalogs (`.dsf.zst`) and coastline/water
masks (`.png`) distributed for ButterSat are licensed under the Open Data
Commons Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0:
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Required attributions for the mesh catalog:
  * Mesh & water vector data: © OpenStreetMap contributors
    (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright), available under ODbL 1.0.
    Derived from OpenStreetMap coastlines (`natural=coastline`), inland water
    polygons, airport boundaries (`aeroway=*`), and road flatten networks.
  * United States elevation data: U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) 3D Elevation
    Program (3DEP) 1/3 arc-second Digital Elevation Model
    (https://www.usgs.gov/3d-elevation-program) — public domain (17 U.S.C. § 105).
  * Global elevation data (outside US): Copernicus DEM GLO-30
    (© DLR e.V. 2010–2014 and © Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014–2018;
    provided under the European Union Copernicus free, full, and open data
    policy).

Note on X-Plane Global Scenery:
  Published catalog DSFs contain zero Laminar Research raster layers (`sim/overlay`
  and `DMED`/`SDME` atoms are stripped prior to publication). At runtime,
  `xof-daemon` splices those raster layers locally on the user's machine from
  the user's own licensed X-Plane 12 Global Scenery installation.


3. Open Regional Orthophoto Imagery (Default Where Available)
-------------------------------------------------------------
Where open government orthophoto coverage exists, ButterSat automatically
selects the open regional provider by default:

  * United States (`usgs`):
    U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) The National Map (`USGSImageryOnly` — USDA
    FSA NAIP 1 m and USGS High Resolution Orthoimagery).
    License: Public domain (17 U.S.C. § 105; USGS data have no copyright or
    licensing restrictions).
    Attribution: "Imagery: U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) The National Map
    (3DEP / NAIP, public domain)".

  * France (`ign`):
    Institut national de l'information géographique et forestière (IGN) —
    Géoplateforme `HR.ORTHOIMAGERY.ORTHOPHOTOS` (BD ORTHO 20 cm).
    License: Licence Ouverte / Open Licence v2.0 (Etalab 2.0).
    Attribution: "Imagery © IGN France — Géoplateforme BD ORTHO (Licence
    Ouverte / Open Licence Etalab 2.0)".

  * Switzerland & Liechtenstein (`swisstopo`):
